Pinned upstream revision: 85f7c3b959a908ed5232ede4f1a4ac7eafe6b630
Revision: https://github.com/ange-yaghi/engine-sim/commit/85f7c3b959a908ed5232ede4f1a4ac7eafe6b630
License: MIT; full copyright and permission notice in LICENSE at this repository root (upstream copy: https://github.com/ange-yaghi/engine-sim/blob/85f7c3b959a908ed5232ede4f1a4ac7eafe6b630/LICENSE).

The EngineSimCore target retains selected upstream src/*.cpp files explicitly listed in Package.swift and their include/ headers. It also uses the original assets/engines/atg-video-2/07_gm_ls.mr and assets/engines/atg-video-2/08_ferrari_f136_v8.mr as the source for the new swift/ls_v8_builder.cpp and swift/f136_v8_builder.cpp C++ ports. The new swift/ls_v8_impulse_response.cpp and swift/f136_v8_impulse_response.cpp embed bytes from assets/sound-library/smooth/smooth_39.wav and es/sound-library/new/mild_exhaust_reverb.wav respectively. These profile ports and embedded sounds retain the upstream engine-sim MIT notice.

Relative to the pinned engine-sim revision, the retained upstream files changed for this package and bridge are include/constants.h, include/gas_system.h, include/units.h, src/connecting_rod.cpp, src/engine.cpp, src/function.cpp, src/jitter_filter.cpp, src/piston_engine_simulator.cpp, src/simulator.cpp, and src/synthesizer.cpp. These changes support Clang compilation, native lifecycle cleanup, and sound rendering; the original files and modifications remain covered by the engine-sim MIT license.

